<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  POPOPX Mac Node - Developer ID entitlements (default, minimal).

  Sealed into the bundle by Scripts/build-release.sh under the hardened runtime.

  Scope: this app is a single Swift Mach-O. It listens on TCP (local web console,
  LAN relay), talks to loopback services, and launches external programs
  (popopx-chat, brew, ollama) resolved from PATH. It does no in-process JIT, no
  dlopen, and loads no embedded dylib or helper: there is nothing under
  Contents/ but the executable, Info.plist, PkgInfo and AppIcon.icns.

  So the hardened runtime escape hatches are deliberately absent:
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
  disable-library-validation would let any unsigned dylib be mapped into this
  process, and allow-unsigned-executable-memory would relax W^X, with no code
  path here that needs either. Entitlements are per-process: the relay and chat
  daemons are separate executables installed elsewhere on PATH, governed by
  their own signatures, so granting these keys here would not help them run. It
  would only widen this app's attack surface.

  When the permissive variant is genuinely required (a runtime embedded inside
  the bundle), select Scripts/entitlements-permissive.plist explicitly through
  the entitlements flag of build-release.sh.

  Note: the two network keys are App Sandbox keys. This bundle is not sandboxed
  (the sandbox would block the LAN listener), so today they are inert, kept to
  declare intent and to survive a future enablement. What actually constrains
  the process is the hardened runtime, not this file.

  Keep this comment free of a double hyphen: it is illegal inside XML, plutil
  -lint accepts it anyway, and codesign's AMFI parser rejects the file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
